cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TGA in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "TGA - Taxo Genomics Analyses: an integrated pipeline for genome-based bacterial taxonomy"
abstract: >-
  TGA takes a folder of bacterial genome assemblies and, in one local run, computes genome quality
  (size, GC, N50, CheckM2), species delineation (ANI with FastANI, dDDH with GBDP formula 2), genus
  delineation (AAI with EzAAI, POCP with DIAMOND) and a rooted phylogenomic tree on the 120 bac120
  marker genes (EasyCGTree, FastTree), with figures and a local web interface.
authors:
  - family-names: Njahi
    given-names: Oussama
    affiliation: "Institut des Régions Arides (IRA), Médenine, Tunisia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Oussama-Njahi/Genome-Taxonomy-Pipeline"
keywords:
  - bacterial taxonomy
  - average nucleotide identity
  - digital DNA-DNA hybridization
  - average amino acid identity
  - percentage of conserved proteins
  - phylogenomics
